- Arithmetic uses [38;5;10mwrapping_*[0m so signed overflow wraps as it does in practice under gcc instead of panicking. Rust's [38;5;10m%[0m on [38;5;10mi32[0m truncates toward zero like C's, so [38;5;10mtemp_buffer[i] % 1000[0m needed no adjustment.[0m[0m
